window.__UPDX=window.__UPDX||{};window.__UPDX["en"] = {"2026-11-23-v727":{"t":"Lighter pages, labels in Russian, rooftops","s":"Every page used to download the whole update log; it now loads only on the Updates page, so the other pages are lighter. A few labels that were empty on the Russian pages are back.","n":["The Russian home page shows 'Latest update' and the entry type again","Rooftops by King's Tower: bitumen caps and metal doors on the roof exits, vent stacks and TV aerials (typical for 2011, placed at random)","Balconies on apartment blocks are drawn a little further from the tower"]},"2026-11-22-v726":{"t":"Full audit of the phone and computer versions","s":"All 9 pages in 4 languages, on a phone and a computer, light and dark: no script errors, no missing files, no dead links, no sideways scrolling.","n":["The quiz photo no longer covers its author and licence line","The home picture is downloaded once (before, phones and computers fetched both the evening and the current version)","The version badge on the Updates page showed v7.0; it now shows the latest version by itself","The accent colour in the light theme is a shade darker so small orange text reads well"]},"2026-11-21-v725":{"t":"Livelier page-head pictures at night and dusk","s":"The renders at the top of the inner pages are no longer near-black at night: the dark is moonlit and the lamps glow; the dusk ones have more contrast and colour.","n":[]},"2026-11-21-v724":{"t":"Engine sound in the window seat, finger hints","s":"With sound on, the From a plane view now has the engine roar through the hull and a faint fan whine; the city noise falls away.","n":["On a touch screen the 3D quarter hint talks about fingers instead of the mouse and Shift"]},"2026-11-21-v723":{"t":"The site on a phone","s":"A pass over every page on a 360–390 px screen.","n":["Fixed: whole blocks on the home page (the story, the timeline) stayed invisible because two scroll animations clashed; this affected computers too","The home render is shorter and its caption readable; the title no longer slides under the picture","The language offer is a slim bar at the bottom that slides away as you scroll, instead of a box over the text","The 3D quarter tools are one row you swipe, with finger-size buttons","Bigger tap targets in the footer menu, no text under 11.5 px, the page name in the header hides on narrow screens"]},"2026-11-20-v722":{"t":"A sharper King's Tower scene and a cinematic window seat","s":"The live scene on the home page now has sun shadows, a colour grade and a closer, lower view of the tower. The From a plane view is now a banked turn round the tower, seen from a cabin window.","n":["Shadows by the sun on the home page as well; on a slow graphics card they switch themselves off","A film-like colour grade: softer greens, cool shadows, warm light, a light vignette","Brick by brick colour on the tower, shadow lines under the sill bands, curtains and tulle in the windows by day","Walls are darker near the ground, flat roofs have bitumen strips and patches","The plane turns round the tower at 200–270 m with a slight bank and light turbulence; the wing has slats, flaps, a winglet, a red navigation light and the engine","The cabin wall, the window reveal and the blind are drawn over the scene; slower than a real airliner, an illustration"]},"2026-11-20-v721":{"t":"Airliners over King's Tower and a passenger's window","s":"Now and then a twin-jet crosses the sky over the King's Tower scene. The new From a plane button puts you in a window seat on a slow circle round the tower, with the wing outside.","n":["The planes fly about four times slower than a real airliner on approach, so the city can be looked at","A generic shape and livery with no airline: this is an illustration, not a record of 2011 flights","At night they carry red and green wing lights and a white strobe","Any drag, click or key returns you to the normal view"]},"2026-11-19-v720":{"t":"Watercolour is the main look of the 3D model","s":"The 3D quarter on the Reconstruction page is now drawn as a watercolour by default: ink lines, washes, pigment grain and paper. The geometry and data are the same.","n":["The Watercolour button turns this view off, and the site remembers it","In evidence mode the model is shown without the style, as before"]},"2026-11-19-v719":{"t":"Trams on the real 2011 routes","s":"Each tram route on the reference map was checked by its own agent, in three passes with fixes. The trams no longer wander at random: each runs its own route.","n":["Routes 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10 and 11 run on the map, through the ДМЗ, Krasnoarmiiska and Gorkoho terminus loops and on past the map edge","Route 12 was reserve-only and route 14 had no service in 2011, so they are not on the map","Missing pieces of track at the map edge on Leninskyi Avenue and Krasnooktiabrska are added","Stops are on the right side and in both directions; routes 3 and 4 board at their own pole, routes 5 and 8 at theirs","Trams no longer halt 2.5 m short of a stop or vanish from the map; passing cars on Postysheva no longer overlap","In the No. 1 cab ride the stop “Dzerzhynskoho Square” is now “Dzerzhynskoho Avenue”, as in OSM 2012"]},"2026-11-18-v718":{"t":"3D model: fixes and live pictures in the page heads","s":"I went over the whole reference map of Donetsk and fixed what looked like a bug. The page heads now show fresh renders of the map in today's light.","n":["Pond and reservoir shores follow the mapped outline instead of the teeth of the 20 m grid; a strip of bank runs along the water","The spoil heap is dark only on the cone itself; the flat stain at the second heap, where the terrain barely rises, is gone","School yards mapped as playgrounds are grass now, not one big sand field","Wet meadows by the streams are green instead of pale squares","The heads of Reconstruction, Development, Updates and Press show renders of the current reference map: the day one by day, the dusk one at sunset, the night one at night"]},"2026-11-18-v717":{"t":"New “Donetsk sunset” palette and a living sky","s":"The site is repainted in a warm palette: sand, graphite and sunset orange. Above the pages a living sky changes with the sun over Donetsk.","n":["The sky behind the page follows the real sun over Donetsk: day, golden hour, sunset, blue dusk","Above every footer, a strip of the project's own render of King's Tower and the Kalmius: the day shot by day, the dusk one at sunset, the night one at night","Sections and cards ease in as you scroll; cards lift with a warm glow on hover","Buttons, the reading bar and the section numbers carry the sunset gradient","The dark theme is a coal-black night with amber accents; with reduced motion the animations are off"]},"2026-11-18-v716":{"t":"Site audit: small fixes","s":"A full check of all 126 pages on desktop and phone and of every 3D scene. The pages have no errors; what turned up is fixed.","n":["In the tram cab the “Photos of this place” chip no longer overlaps the time-of-day button","If the graphics card drops the 3D model, a still of the quarter and a “Start again” button appear instead of a black box"]},"2026-11-18-v715":{"t":"Shadows across the whole city","s":"On the reference map every house, tree and hill now casts a shadow wherever the camera looks, not only in the quarter.","n":["Shadows follow the camera: 220 m to 1.3 km around the view point (phones keep the old behaviour for speed)","Streams and rivers lie on the ground instead of hanging over hollows","Traffic lights, bus shelters and kiosks no longer sink into the ground","Aerials and lift rooms no longer float in the air beside L-shaped blocks"]},"2026-11-18-v714":{"t":"Reference map: a sector-by-sector audit","s":"The 4.4×2.8 km map of Donetsk was checked in four sectors: buildings, transport, ground and water, objects and camera. What floated, sank, flickered or stood in the wrong place is fixed.","n":["Roads and tracks follow the terrain and no longer cut into hills; bridges have decks with a parapet and railing","Overhead-line poles and street lamps moved off the carriageway (about 400); tracks show ballast, sleepers and rails","Walls reach the ground on slopes; private houses have hip roofs, factory halls have windows and roof lights","At night windows are lit across the whole map, not only around the tower","The map no longer ends in a void: the edge fades into haze; pond shores are smooth, without steps","Trees no longer stand on roads, rails or in water; the private-house sector has gardens (positions illustrative)","The camera no longer goes under the ground on hills; street names no longer overlap","Cars no longer stand inside houses, fences no longer block roads, chimney stacks have realistic thickness"]},"2026-11-14-v713":{"t":"3D audit: fewer artifacts","s":"Every 3D scene on the site was checked. What shimmered, flickered or looked unnatural is fixed.","n":["After you return to the tab the scene no longer loses its shadows and reflections; the daytime scene is brighter","Distant roads and markings no longer flicker when zoomed out (in all three scenes)","The tower's facade does not shimmer from afar: distant windows blend into an even tone, and brick courses show only up close","From above trees look like crowns, not crosses; from the side they look as before","Tree shadows are crown-shaped patches, not stripes","Parked cars no longer stand inside one another","King's Tower in the reference map now really loads: browsers kept the old model file"]},"2026-11-13-v712":{"t":"King's Tower in the reference map","s":"In the 3D model on the Reconstruction page King's Tower is no longer a brown box: it now uses the same detailed model as the live scene — the oval plan, brick piers and cream loggias, windows on every floor, glazed top floors, the crown and the mast.","n":["In the evening some of the tower's windows are lit","In evidence mode the tower stays a plain OSM outline"]},"2026-11-13-v711":{"t":"A living map you can walk around","s":"The 3D scene at King's Tower is no longer tied to the tower: you can move the map across the whole district and double-click to fly anywhere. Trams run on the tram tracks, and birds circle over the water and the yards.","n":["Move the map: right mouse button, Shift or two fingers; keys W A S D; Home returns to the tower","View buttons: Tower, Embankment, Tram, From above","The camera moves smoothly","Tatra T3 trams in red and cream run on the district's tracks; none between 1 and 5 at night","Flocks of birds by day in clear weather","Distant water is calmer, without repeating stripes","Trams and birds, like the cars and people, are a simulation, not a record of 2011"]},"2026-11-09-v710":{"t":"Tram: small fixes","s":"The cab view was checked on a computer with a GeForce card: it starts and rides without crashes. Small issues found during the check are fixed.","n":["After jumping to a stop or dragging the slider, the trip clock shows how long a real ride to that point takes","In the cab view the photo button is smaller and sits in the corner, off the road"]},"2026-11-05-v79":{"t":"Cab view: houses and stops","s":"The buildings along the line look closer to the real ones: the five-storey panel blocks show the joints between panels, window reveals and curtains, and the private houses got windows in white frames and brick courses. The stops have a tiled platform with a yellow edge, a bench and a bin.","n":["Taller buildings with flat roofs have a parapet along the edge","The panels of each block differ slightly in tone, as after years of repairs","The colours are a little livelier and warmer in the sun"]},"2026-11-02-v78":{"t":"The cab view works on Windows computers","s":"On some graphics cards under Windows (tested on a GeForce GTX 980 Ti) the tram cab view crashed the graphics driver while starting, and the browser then switched off 3D for the site. The cause is found: one shader drew the street and the trees together and was too complex for the driver's compiler. The trees now have their own small shader, and the cab starts.","n":["If the browser still has 3D switched off after an old crash, quit the browser completely and open it again"]},"2026-11-02-v77":{"t":"Living trees, and a live tower on the home page","s":"The 3D trees are no longer plastic: ten species of Donetsk streets in October — columnar and spreading poplars, lindens, chestnuts, maples, birches, black locusts and willows by the water — painted leaf by leaf with trunk and branches, swaying in the wind. And on a computer the home page now opens with the live King's Tower scene instead of a picture.","n":["Cab view of the tram: the new trees and soft shadows under the crowns","King's Tower in 3D: the new trees close up and to the horizon; the near trees are ten times lighter for the graphics card","Home page: the scene circles the tower slowly, with the sun and the lit windows as they are in Donetsk right now; phones and weak graphics keep the picture"]},"2026-11-01-v76":{"t":"The cab view: a living sky, rails and trees","s":"The ride on route 1 is closer to the real thing: clouds and sun in the sky, sleepers and ballast under the wheels, autumn trees with leafy crowns and a Tatra cab with an instrument panel.","n":["A sky with drifting clouds, the sun and haze on the horizon; stars at night","The track: ballast, concrete sleepers, rust beside the rails and bright worn rail heads","Late-October grass with fallen leaves, patched asphalt, water that mirrors the sky","Tree crowns built from clumps of leaves with gaps, not flat discs","The cab: window pillars, a sun visor, dusty glass outside the wiper's sweep, a speedometer and switch panel; a generalised Tatra T3SU cab"]},"2026-11-01-v75":{"t":"The cab view no longer disappears","s":"If the graphics card drops 3D, or the browser blocks it after a crash, the cab button stays: the tram rides on in the photo view, a note says why 3D did not start, and a button tries again.","n":["When the browser has blocked 3D after a graphics-driver crash, the site says so plainly: quit the browser completely and open it again","The King's Tower 3D scene explains a graphics-card failure instead of showing a black screen","On a slow graphics card the scene drops shadows and reflections at once when frames start to stall"]},"2026-10-31-v74":{"t":"A direct link to King's Tower in 3D","s":"The short address gek2or.github.io/donetsk-2011/3d opens the 3D scene at once, in the visitor's language: handy for the link in an Instagram bio.","n":["The home page with #3d opens the scene at once too; closing the scene restores the plain address","The flat top cards of the distant trees are smaller and no longer show from the side"]},"2026-10-30-v73":{"t":"King's Tower in 3D: the city to the horizon","s":"The scene around the tower is no longer empty: the whole 4.4 × 2.8 km district with every house, street, fence and track from OpenStreetMap, and about 30,000 trees by land use.","n":["All 4,636 buildings of the district, not only the near ones; the far ones are drawn simpler","Every street of the district, fences, tram and railway tracks, sports pitches, factory chimneys, tanks and the water tower","Trees: the yards of the blocks of flats and the gardens of the private houses are thick, parks and tree belts thicker still, willows and poplars by the water; an autumn mix of green, yellow and russet. Tree groups follow the map, the spot of each tree is an estimate","The ground is coloured by land use across the district: industry, lawns, parks, woods; patches of dry October grass","Parked cars within 900 m, traffic on the streets within a kilometre","Phones get a lighter scene: buildings to 1.4 km and up to 9,000 trees, so it stays smooth"]},"2026-10-29-v72":{"t":"Project motto: “The map must be like the real thing”; King's Tower on the real relief","s":"The project now has a motto, and it is on the home page, the Development page, the press kit and the 3D scenes. The first step under it: the King's Tower scene stands on the real relief instead of a flat plane.","n":["The motto “The map must be like the real thing”: every street, house, tree and fence stands where it really stood, and where exact data is missing, it is marked as an estimate","The relief around the tower comes from the SRTM radar survey: the city rises to the west, towards Kovalya St and beyond, and falls about 15 metres to the reservoir","The tower yard is a level platform at the height of its ground floor, as on the October 2011 panoramas; towards the lower street it ends in a retaining wall with a parapet","On the south-east and east the ground is 2–4 metres lower, and the tower's grey-tiled lower storey with windows shows; steps with red railings climb from the street to the yard","The bank runs down to the water as a grassy slope; houses, trees, lamps, cars and people stand on the ground of their own spot","SRTM relief is accurate to about 1–5 m; the north side of the yard has no panoramas, so the transition there is smooth and estimated"]},"2026-10-29-v71":{"t":"King's Tower in 3D: the yard and the embankment from October 2011 panoramas","s":"The area around the tower is now checked against Street View panoramas taken in October 2011 and a fresh OpenStreetMap extract: the car park, the playground, the lower street with its fences, the waste ground, the embankment with willows.","n":["Google's panoramas around the tower were taken in October 2011 itself; objects are placed by them, the images themselves never go into the scene","The yard to the west: a marked car park with a guard booth, a playground behind a low green fence (slide, swings, climbing frame, sandpit), globe lamps by the tower","Kovalya St had young staked saplings in 2011, and so does the scene now","The lower street to the south: a parapet on the car park's retaining wall, tiled pavement, profiled-sheet fences (grey and one blue), concrete poles with wires, steps with red railings at the tower","To the north-west, waste ground with dry grass behind a sheet-metal fence; a concrete fence across Kovalya St","The embankment: weeping willows and white poplars by the water, dense groups of trees, an anchor chain on low posts along the path; the bank is grass down to the water","The sports hall on the embankment is now blue, like its cladding in 2011; green bins and a blue container by the east driveway","From OSM: more car parks, the kindergarten fence, the 'Palace of Sport Dynamo' bus stop, zebra crossings on the avenue, the dam crest","Positions taken from the panoramas are estimates (2–5 m); tree groups follow the crowns on the imagery, single trees are approximate"]},"2026-10-29-v70":{"t":"King's Tower in 3D: a living block on the Kalmius","s":"The home page has a new 'King's Tower in 3D' button: rotate and zoom around the tower while the block around it goes about its day.","n":["At the tower: sills and lintels in relief, air conditioners, slab edges on the loggias, a paved apron around it (typical); different lamps, curtains and flickering TVs in the windows; Soviet street lamps; benches and bins at the entrances (typical); people stride, walk in pairs and carry umbrellas in the rain; soft shadows at the walls and under the trees; a glow around the lights at night","More detail around the tower: trees with branches and autumn leaves (chestnut, linden, poplar, maple, birch, acacia), private houses with hip roofs and chimneys, balconies and entrances of the blocks of flats, raised pavements with kerbs, road markings, the sloping river bank","Sun and shadows follow the Donetsk clock or a slider; speed up time to watch windows, street lamps and the tower floodlights come on","Cars drive on the OpenStreetMap streets, with headlights at night; people walk the pavements and the embankment","The water reflects the tower and the lights and ripples in the wind; rain and fog on a button","A quiet city sound made right in the browser: traffic, wind, water, rain","The scene loads only when asked, so the home page is no heavier","The tower, houses, streets and water follow OpenStreetMap, photos and public listings; traffic, people, lit windows and weather are a simulation"]},"2026-10-28-v69":{"t":"Home: King's Tower over the Kalmius","s":"The first screen now shows a new render of King's Tower and the Kalmius reservoir. The picture follows the time in Donetsk: day, evening, night.","n":["The tower is built from the OpenStreetMap outline, the 109 m height and 29 floors from public listings, and photographs; facade details are approximate","The night view follows a photo from the far bank: facade floodlighting, the red light on the mast, lights on the water","Rendered in Blender (Cycles) with 4,500 OSM buildings, roads and water around it; the far horizon is generic","Fixed: the 'Read in Russian' link on the other-language pages led back to the same page","Postcard: the greeting and small captions have more contrast","On phones, buttons and links are now at least 24 pixels","The updates page shows the real site version"]},"2026-10-23-v68":{"t":"Tram 1: rails and oncoming trams where they belong","s":"Fixed the track geometry in the cab view: no more doubled rails, the oncoming tram runs on the second track, and cars and pedestrians stay off the tram tracks.","n":["Trees no longer stand on the rails: 372 removed from the tracks, 186 given smaller crowns so they do not overhang the line","Our own track is drawn only from the route line; duplicate OSM tracks within 2.4 m are removed","The second track is measured from OSM every 4 m; the oncoming tram follows it exactly and does not appear where there is no second track","The oncoming tram now faces us, headlights first","Cars on one-way carriageways drive only in the permitted direction, centred in their half","Cars and pedestrians never appear within 2.6–2.7 m of the rails","Catenary poles only stand on free ground: not on the carriageway, the second track or inside buildings; a long bracket spans both tracks, and on wide streets a cross-span wire runs between poles on both sides (before: 126 of 330 poles stood on the road)","Street lamps move away from rails, roads and walls; where there is no room there is no lamp (before: about 300 of 3091 stood on tracks, roads or in buildings)","Stops: a platform only where the ground on the right is free; on streets people wait on the pavement past the kerb, not on a platform in the middle of the road","Where the track runs in the carriageway and at level crossings it lies in concrete slabs instead of ballast","Trees: 318 trunks inside buildings and 120 on carriageways removed; crowns next to walls narrowed so they no longer pass through walls","Home: a fourth way in under “Start here” — the cab ride on tram route 1","Section descriptions no longer mention the Zarichna walk, which is gone from the site","Press kit: the site description now includes the tram ride, the October 2011 chronicle and the radio"]},"2026-10-22-v67":{"t":"Tram No. 1: 2012 shop signs and passers-by","s":"The buildings along the route now carry the signs of shops, cafés, bars and banks, and people walk along the pavements.","n":["84 signs from OpenStreetMap as of 13 September 2012: McDonald's, Velyka Kyshenia, the Yuzovka brewery pub, Chicago, the main post office, the Planeta mall and more","Where a place had no name in 2012, it carries a plain sign for its kind: Pharmacy, Groceries, Flowers","The signs light up at night","Passers-by walk along the pavements of the main streets","The ride is slower: twice real time by default, and you can ride in real time too (the ×1, ×2, ×5, ×15 button)"],"i":[]},"2026-10-21-v66":{"t":"Tram No. 1: the view from the cab","s":"The ride now shows the city from the driver’s seat: houses, streets, trees, poles and the overhead wire along all 11 kilometres of the route.","n":["A 3D cab view from OpenStreetMap data along the whole line: 3,300 buildings, streets with markings and pavements, parks and water","Rails, the contact wire and its poles, platforms and shelters at the stops","A dashboard: speedometer, controller, door, run and brake lamps","Relief from SRTM data: the climbs and descents along the way","October trees along the streets and in the yards, cars on the streets, trams passing the other way","Street lamps, loggias on the five- and nine-storey blocks, people waiting at the stops","Time of day: now in Donetsk, day, evening or night; at night the windows, street lamps and headlights are lit","When a 2008–2013 photo was taken nearby, a button lets you look at it","The streets come from the current map; buildings put up in 2012 or later are removed"],"i":[]},"2026-10-21-v65":{"t":"Tram No. 1 now runs on the real track","s":"The ride on route 1 is rebuilt: the tram follows the route’s rails from OpenStreetMap, speeds up, slows for the curves and waits at the stops. The “Then and later” section is gone.","n":["The path is the real route 1 line, 11.2 km, instead of straight lines between the stops","A destination board, speed, distance covered and travel time (an estimate, not a timetable)","A route diagram like the one inside the car: all 26 stops, tap any of them","The window shows 2008–2013 photos taken next to the line; where there are none, a view from above on the map","You can ride four times faster","The “Then and later” section with photos from after 2014 is removed from the site and the atlas"],"i":[]},"2026-10-21-v64":{"t":"A new look for the “Do you remember where this is?” game, and a clearer home page","s":"The game now opens the City page: a dark stage with a stack of photos, a single Play button and the four modes as cards. The home page has a new “Start here” block.","n":["The game modes are cards that say what to do, how many rounds there are and your record","Play starts a game straight away; Photo of the day shows the day number and your streak","At the end of a game, a strip of all eight photos shows which ones you got right","You can answer with the 1–4 keys and press Enter to go on","The game comes first on the City page; it used to sit below the photo archive","The home page has three ways in: the game, the 3D model of the district and the photo archive"],"i":[]},"2026-10-20-v63":{"t":"Roads and traffic: widths from lanes, surfaces, 700 cars, tail lights","s":"The roads of the reference map are reworked. Carriageway widths come from the number of lanes and surfaces come from OSM. Traffic is denser and behaves better at junctions.","n":["Carriageway widths follow the OSM lane count rather than the road class. Each half of a dual carriageway is no longer drawn 14 m wide. Markings, pavements, lamps, shelters, signals and trolleybus wires follow this width","Surfaces from the OSM tag: dirt streets of the private sector, cobbles, concrete","Tram tracks laid in the carriageway are drawn without ballast, rails straight on the asphalt (19 stretches)","Up to 700 cars instead of 380, more of them on the main streets; at the morning rush hour the average speed is about 20 km/h","At a junction without signals a car holds it until it has passed, the others wait at the edge","Cars no longer jump between lanes when they pass a node; they turn smoothly","Red tail lights at night"],"i":[]},"2026-10-19-v62":{"t":"First storey counts from the 2011 panoramas; a lighter map for phones","s":"A pass over the Google Street View panoramas taken in October 2011 has begun. Storeys are counted by eye and written into the project; the images themselves never reach the site. The building card marks such a height as class B.","n":["Four buildings have storey counts from the panoramas: Kobozieva 4; Horkoho 61 (seen from Cheliuskintsiv Street); Artema 63 and Artema 71","On phones and low-memory devices the map is built lighter: half the trees, no cars in the yards and no entrance details","3D map audit: entrances now sit on the actual walls of the blocks rather than on their bounding box; trees, cars and wagons that ended up inside buildings or on roads are removed","The map takes about 140 MB of memory instead of almost 600 MB and opens faster","The Bis residential tower is removed: OSM dates its construction to 2012","Cars run into each other less often at junctions without signals","The river is no longer drawn as a strip across the reservoir; the spoil heap slope is no longer a flat stain","The evidence-mode legend now covers grade B; the traffic notes in the map card fold under \"Traffic and map details\"","October 2011 in colour: about a quarter of the crowns are already yellow and rust, almost half of the birches (illustrative)","People wait at the bus and tram stops, one to three by each shelter","The card of a building with storeys from a panorama now gives the storey count","A soft contact shadow at the foot of the larger buildings, so they no longer seem to hover over the ground"],"i":[]},"2026-10-19-v61":{"t":"The 3D opens on the reference map; markets, petrol stations, fountains, balconies","s":"The 3D model now opens straight on the whole 4.37 × 2.84 km reference map. The Zarechna Street quarter stays at its centre; to go back to the quarter alone, switch off the \"Reference map\" button. The map has more small things of the city, at the places OSM marks them.","n":["About 190 market stalls with striped awnings at the Zhovtnevyi and Slovianskyi markets","About 340 cars in the open car parks","Pumps under the canopies of three petrol stations","Three fountains with a basin and a jet, the musical fountain among them","Swings, slides and sandboxes on the playgrounds, goals on the football pitches","Kiosks by about half of the bus stops","Balconies on the facades of the apartment blocks; pedestrians now walk instead of gliding","Entrances of the apartment blocks: a concrete canopy, a door, a bench and a lamp over the door that lights up in the evening (illustrative)","Shelters at the tram stops mapped in OSM 2012","Freight wagons — gondolas, tank cars, box cars — on the industrial spurs (illustrative)","Brick chimneys on the roofs of private houses, TV aerials on the roofs of the apartment blocks (illustrative)","The places come from OSM; the stalls, cars, swings and kiosks themselves are placed illustratively"],"i":[]},"2026-10-19-v60":{"t":"The 3D map comes alive: trolleybuses, pedestrians, power lines, street trees","s":"The reference map has more life and more city in it. Trolleybuses under their wires, pedestrians on the pavements, high-voltage lines, factory chimneys, trees along the main streets and cars in the yards are added. The map card says which of it rests on data and which is placed illustratively.","n":["Trolleybus overhead wires over the streets of the routes: Artema, Leninskyi prospekt, Universytetska; trolleybuses with their poles run under them and stop at the stops","Pedestrians on the pavements of the main streets; at signalled junctions they cross at the zebras while the cars have red","35 and 110 kV power lines from OSM: lattice towers and sagging wires","Factory chimneys with red and white bands, the water tower, the dark slope of the Tsentralno-Zavodska mine spoil heap","About 6,600 street trees: chestnuts and lindens, Lombardy poplars, birches (placement illustrative)","About 2,500 cars parked along the drives in the yards of the apartment blocks (illustrative)","Windows on large buildings with a known storey count, dark flat roofs, railings on the bridges"],"i":[]},"2026-10-18-v59":{"t":"A fuller reference map: fences, colours, storeys, yards","s":"The reference map is noticeably fuller. Everything OpenStreetMap already has but was not drawn before is now on it. Where there is no data, some gaps are filled with careful estimates, and each of them is labelled.","n":["771 fences and walls from OSM: private-sector plots, industrial sites, schools and hospitals are enclosed as the map shows","Wall and roof colours from OSM tags on 333 buildings: brick red, cream, grey","211 large buildings without a storey count take their height from nearby buildings of the same shape whose storeys are known; the card marks this as an estimate","38 sports pitches and playgrounds, 9 storage tanks","About 2,400 trees in the yards of private houses, on the side of the plot away from the street (illustrative)","36 street names on the map instead of 16"],"i":[]},"2026-10-17-v58":{"t":"Lighter and more detailed 3D: pavements, stops, roofs","s":"The model is now half as heavy for the graphics card. The reference map draws only what is in view, and small details only up close. The headroom went into pavements, bus shelters and the roofs of the blocks of flats.","n":["Normals, colours and facade coordinates are stored compactly: the geometry takes about half the memory","The map is split into 500 × 500 m tiles: tiles outside the view are skipped, and trees, lamps, markings and pavements are skipped beyond 1.1 km from the camera","Pavements with a kerb along the main streets; none on the medians of the avenues","Bus shelters at the 38 bus stops from OSM 2012","Parapets on the flat roofs of blocks of flats, and lift machine rooms on blocks of nine storeys and more","The pavements, shelters and roofs follow a typical layout, not photos of each building"],"i":[]},"2026-10-17-v57":{"t":"Streets of the reference map: markings, zebras, lamps and trees","s":"The streets of the reference map are more detailed now. The main roads have lane markings, the signals have stop lines and zebras, the avenues have lamps that come on in the evening, the parks and woods have trees, and the tram tracks have their overhead line.","n":["A dashed centre line and lane dividers on the main streets; road joints at bends and junctions without gaps","Zebras and stop lines before every signal, plus 16 crossings where OSM had them in 2012","About 1,800 lamps along the main streets; after sunset they light up, and cars and trams have their headlights on","Trees in the woods and parks shown on the map, and poles with the contact wire over the tram tracks","The markings, lamps and trees follow a typical layout, not photos of each street"],"i":[]},"2026-10-17-v56":{"t":"The reference map comes alive: cars, trams and traffic lights","s":"The reference map now runs a small street-traffic simulation. Cars, minibuses, buses and trams drive its streets, stopping at red lights and at stops. The signals and stops stand where OpenStreetMap had them by September 2012, the earliest state of the map the OSM history keeps and the closest to 2011.","n":["29 signalled junctions with 87 signal heads: green, amber, red and an all-red pause between phases","38 bus and 29 tram stops from OSM 2012; buses and trams wait at them for 11–18 seconds","Up to 380 cars, GAZelle minibuses, yellow buses and Tatra T3 trams; one-way streets and lane counts come from OSM","Traffic follows the hour on the sun slider: the streets are almost empty at night and busier in the rush hours","The cars, their routes and the signal timing are illustrative: a model, not a record of real traffic","A register of storey counts from 2011 Street View panoramas is ready; buildings checked against a panorama will get class B"],"i":[]},"2026-10-17-v55":{"t":"The next ring: the reference map in 3D","s":"The project grows in rings: a house, a corridor, the quarter, the reference map, the district, the city. The browser 3D model now opens the third ring. Around the Zarichna quarter rise 4.37 × 2.84 km of the city, with Artema and Postysheva streets, Komsomolskyi Avenue, the Kalmius and the city ponds.","n":["4,638 buildings on their OpenStreetMap outlines; 1,512 take their height from storeys or the height tag, the rest stand at a height typical for their type, marked as an estimate","Streets of every class, the railway and tram tracks, bridges, the Kalmius and Bakhmutka rivers, the Central and Second City Ponds, the Nyzhniokalmiuske reservoir, parks, woods and industrial zones","Only what is on the map: trees stand where OSM marks them, and buildings of unknown use get no invented windows","Tap any building on the map: type, height, where the height comes from, and a link to the object in OSM","The map loads only when you press “Reference map”, so the page itself stays light","SRTM relief for the whole map arrives with the next site update; until then the terrain outside the quarter is a placeholder"],"i":[]},"2026-10-17-v54":{"t":"3D quarter: garages, substations and yards","s":"I checked the quarter’s models against the building types in OpenStreetMap. Until now everything that was not a house stood there as a house with a gable roof. Garages, substations, the canopy and outbuildings now look like what they are, and plots and yards have proper ground.","n":["Garage rows are low, with flat roofs and a gate every 3.3 m, each gate a different colour","The 110 kV substation “Kalmiuska” is a two-storey brick hall with window bands and a gate; the transformer kiosk is a brick box with two steel doors and a yellow plate","The canopy over the drive stands on posts, not walls","House plots have a lawn in front, a vegetable garden behind and a paved path; the garage cooperative is asphalted; the blocks of flats have lawns and paths","The five-storey block at 38 Donetska no longer has a lift room on its roof: such blocks had no lifts. The roofs of both blocks get vent stacks and TV aerials","The building card shows the type and where it comes from, the OSM tags or a guess from the footprint and address, and the height the building is drawn at"],"i":[]},"2026-10-12-v43":{"t":"A walk down Zarichna, tram No. 1, a radio and postcards","s":"You can now walk through the 3D quarter yourself, at eye level. The city page lets you ride the whole tram No. 1 route, the sound page has an old receiver with “stations” to tune into, and you can send a friend a postcard from 2011.","n":["First-person walk: keys or a joystick on phones, a sky with the sun and stars, autumn trees, the address of the house in your sights and a mini-map. Houses don’t let you walk through, windows and street lamps light up in the evening, birds sing by day and crickets at night","Panorama hunt: six spots where a Street View camera stood in October 2011 are marked with beams of light. The ones you find are remembered only on your device","Tram No. 1 from the railway station to the steelworks: 26 stops on the map, a stop display, the view from the window and sound made in the browser","Radio “Donetsk 2011”: a tuning knob, static between stations and six “stations” made of city sounds","A postcard from 2011: a photo, a stamp and a few handwritten lines; the envelope opens for the recipient, and the site stores nothing"],"i":["Photos in the atlas can be sent as a postcard straight away","The Back and Next buttons of the guided walk on the reconstruction page have their labels back"]},"2026-10-11-v42":{"t":"Evening in 3D, October 2011 day by day and place cards","s":"In the 3D quarter you can now wait for sunset: windows and street lamps light up. The city page has a chronicle of October 2011 with daily weather, matches and events. Every atlas place has its own card for social media, and the site itself got lighter.","n":["The sun slider runs to 19:30: sunset at 17:41, dusk, lit windows and street lamps","“October 2011” chronicle: daily temperature and rain from the Donetsk weather station and 16 events of the month, each with its source","A “Share” button on atlas places: the link opens the place on the map and shows a photo card on social media","The atlas now shows 21 of the 22 archive photos"],"i":["Fonts are almost half the size","Page header images in WebP with smaller copies for phones","Parts of a page below the screen are not drawn until you scroll to them, which is easier on phones"]},"2026-10-09-v41":{"t":"Search, the site as an app and facades in 3D","s":"You can now search the site in all four languages. The site can be installed on a phone or computer, and pages you have read open without a connection. Houses in the 3D quarter now have colours and windows.","n":["Search across pages, photos, “Then and later” and the update log: the magnifier button in the menu, the / key or Ctrl+K","Install the site as an app, with offline reading for pages you have opened and photos you have seen","Facades in the 3D quarter: windows, plinths and illustrative materials by building type, with a switch to turn them off","The atlas now shows 15 of the 22 archive photos and all four “Then and later” places"],"i":["The house card names the illustrative facade material and says it is not taken from a photo","Archive photos open full size from the atlas"]},"2026-10-08-guests":{"t":"Site guests, RSS and a living album","s":"The site now has guests: you can see how many times people came here and from which countries. Updates can be followed via RSS, and the album pages came to life.","n":["“Guests of Donetsk 2011” on the home page: the visit count and stamps with country flags","An RSS feed of updates in four languages and a “Follow the project” button","Preview cards for each section when you hover the menu","The “five pillars” hang on a string and flutter like a paper flag"],"i":["The page under the cursor is loaded in advance, so navigation is almost instant","Buttons fill with colour like ink, and a second photo peeks out from behind the section cards","Wikimedia Commons photos are gradually moving onto the site itself: faster and more reliable"]},"2026-10-08-album":{"t":"A new look: a family photo album from 2011","s":"The site no longer looks like a tech template. It now feels like an album you leaf through at home: paper, white-bordered prints, handwritten captions and the orange date of a digital camera on the photos.","n":["Alegreya for headings, Literata for text, handwritten Caveat for captions","Archive photos, Unreal frames and previews as taped prints","The author’s story is laid out as a letter instead of a dark slide","The dark theme is now an album under a lamp, without the cold blue"],"i":["Project figures and milestones are written in the margins instead of grey tiles"]},"2026-10-08-quiz":{"t":"A Donetsk quiz: 53 photos, a city map and a photo of the day","s":"The small 14-photo guessing game is now a full quiz: 53 photos from 2008–2013 of 19 places in the city and four modes.","n":["Where on the map?: put a pin on the map of Donetsk, points depend on the distance","Guess the year: taken before 2011, in 2011 or later","Photo of the day: one photo for everyone, one try and a result in squares for Telegram and Instagram","Shared stats: each photo shows how many players got it right","Readers’ photos: your own 2008–2012 shots can be sent by email, and the best go into the quiz and the archive"],"i":["Guess the place: 19 places instead of 7, from the railway station and the airport to the slag heaps","A new map of the whole city from OpenStreetMap: roads, rivers, ponds, parks"]},"2026-10-07-v34":{"t":"Before/after, a live preview and memories without GitHub","s":"The site shows more: blockout progress is visible with a slider, the home page plays a live model of the quarter, and a memory can now be sent as an ordinary email.","n":["A before/after comparison on the Development page and in the updates feed","A live video of the 3D quarter on the home page that opens the model in one click","Memory map: sending by email without an account, fields for text and signature","Guess the place: after answering you can add a memory of that place straight away"],"i":["The home video is 0.6 MB, loads only when visible and does not play with data saver or reduced motion","The Contact section on the Press page: the author’s email"]},"2026-10-01-press":{"t":"Press kit and faster loading","s":"The site got lighter and easier to share: moving between pages is several times faster and links now show proper previews.","n":["A Press page: description, facts, images and a logo","Link previews for Telegram, Instagram and social networks on every page","A custom 404 page"],"i":["Shared styles and scripts are cached: moving between pages loads 12–35 times less","3D quarter data loads only on Reconstruction","A sitemap and structured data for search engines"]},"2026-09-30-feed":{"t":"The update feed","s":"A new page gathers every change to the game, the site and the research into one feed.","n":["Filter by game, site or research","“New” marks since your last visit and a counter in the menu","A stage rail: where the project is now","A link to every entry and a latest-update card on the home page"]},"2026-09-30-v3":{"t":"The real Donetsk and a model of the quarter","s":"Grey captures gave way to photographs of the city from 2008–2013 and renders of the 3D model lit by the October 2011 sun.","n":["A 22-photo archive with filters and a full-screen viewer","The 3D quarter with shadows and a sun slider set to 15 October 2011","A walk through the 3D model with Back and Next buttons","“Guess the place”: 14 photos, 7 places and a best score"],"i":["A hero image of Donetsk at dusk in November 2011","Development in order: goal, method, engine, blockout, plan, log","Unreal captures gathered in the Blockout section"],"f":["Removed the link to the deleted atlas"]},"2026-09-30-mobile":{"t":"Comfortable on a phone","s":"The mobile version got a pinned menu and tidier typography.","n":["The ☰ menu is pinned to the top of the screen"],"i":["The log shows the last 4 entries on phones","Headings scale to fit the screen width"],"f":["Long words no longer break in the middle","Pages no longer slide sideways on narrow screens"]},"2026-09-30-pages":{"t":"Four pages instead of one","s":"The site is split into Home, The city, Reconstruction and Development. Each page answers its own question.","n":["A page menu and quick links to sections"],"i":["The gist of the atlas moved into the memory map caption"],"f":["Removed repeated blocks"]},"2026-09-28-memory":{"t":"The memory map","s":"Anyone who remembers Donetsk can mark a place on the map and leave a memory.","n":["A 4.37 × 2.84 km map of the centre where you pick a point","Submission through a GitHub form with the place's coordinates","The memory appears on the site after review"]},"2026-09-26-interactive":{"t":"The 3D quarter, a walk and a game","s":"The site became interactive: you can fly over the quarter, walk the street and remember the city in a game.","n":["A 280 × 660 m 3D model of the quarter right in the browser","Evidence mode: every house shows what is known and what is estimated","A walk down Zarichna through 9 panorama points from 2011","The “Guess the place” game and the sound diary shelf"],"i":["“New” marks in the development log"]},"2026-09-25-quarter":{"t":"The working quarter of Zarichna and Donetska","s":"@d29","n":["189 volumes from individual OSM outlines","SRTM terrain under the whole quarter","A continuous 412 m corridor from six panoramas"],"i":["18 surface checks and 38 GIS tests"]},"2026-09-25-osm2012":{"t":"Checking OSM from 2012","s":"@d30"},"2026-09-25-film":{"t":"Why the city is out of reach","s":"The home page gained Davito Daveeni's 2012 film about Donetsk and figures with sources.","n":["A section on why there is no way back to Donetsk","The 2012 documentary with thanks to its author"],"i":["Every figure checked and sourced"]},"2026-09-24-player":{"t":"The first Windows player","s":"@d28","n":["Pause menu, saving and loading","A 54 m facade study at house 33"]},"2026-09-24-launch":{"t":"The site goes live","s":"@d26","n":["Russian, Ukrainian, English and Finnish","A personal story and Street View panoramas from 2011","A photo archive of Donetsk before 2014","A live Donetsk 2011 clock and a ticker of streets"]},"2026-09-23-unreal":{"t":"Moving to Unreal Engine 5.8","s":"@d25"},"2026-09-22-unity":{"t":"The Unity prototype","s":"@d24"},"2026-09-21-panoramas":{"t":"The October 2011 panoramas","s":"@d23"},"2026-09-14-origin":{"t":"The origin point","s":"@d22"},"2026-09-13-osm":{"t":"The reference map of the centre","s":"@d21"},"2026-09-30-north":{"t":"The northern road and the gate from the 2011 panoramas","s":"@d35","n":["7 trees, 10 shrubs and a low wall on the east verge","Scalloped concrete gate panels with relief joints","A low board fence north of label 30"],"i":["A soft dirt-to-asphalt edge at the gate","Shrubs and a tree on the west verge"]},"2026-09-29-planting":{"t":"Planting before the northern building","s":"The October 2011 south view showed dense greenery on the west verge. The model now has four shrubs and a small tree there; the full DX11 run passed 27 checks and 3 routes."},"2026-09-28-north":{"t":"The north of the quarter and the first 67 metres","s":"@d34","n":["A retaining wall, a raised lawn and three conifers","Windows and projecting edges on the end facade","7 trees, 7 shrubs and 4 garden clusters on the first segment"],"i":["Asphalt, patches, dirt and gravel are now separate surfaces"],"f":["Removed a misplaced annex that blocked the service lane"]},"2026-09-25-guided":{"t":"An observation walk in the game","s":"The playable quarter now starts at house 33 and guides the player through six October 2011 panorama points. The HUD shows what is known and what is estimated.","n":["Six steps through the 2011 panorama points","A restrained HUD without money or missions"],"i":["The crowd walks only along the east verge of the quarter","A tool for repeatable drive-through captures"]},"2026-10-08-daynight":{"t":"Day and night on Donetsk time, “Then and later”, a sound diary","s":"The site now lives on Donetsk time: when it is night in Donetsk, the album goes dark. New: a “How to help” page, a sound diary and four places in the city before and after 2014.","n":["A “now in Donetsk” clock in the menu and day and night that follow the sun over the city","“Then and later”: four places before and after 2014 with a time slider","A “How to help” page: photos, memories, the game, a link for friends","A “Sound diary”: a cassette player for future recordings and themes, made without AI"],"i":["The theme button has three modes: Donetsk time, light and dark","Pages turn slightly warmer at dawn and dusk"]},"2026-10-09-v40":{"t":"Atlas, an address per language and faster photos","s":"Every photo on the site is now on one map of the city. Each language has its own address, so search engines find the site in all four languages. Photos are lighter and small text has more contrast.","n":["An atlas on “The city” page: points for every photo and the “Then and later” places, photos on tap","Separate addresses /uk/, /en/, /fi/ with the text already in that language","A quiet hint when the page exists in your browser’s language","A “Skip to content” link for keyboard and screen reader users"],"i":["Photos in WebP with smaller copies for phones: previews are about five times lighter","The script loads the texts of one language only","Small grey text has more contrast","Fonts are served from the site itself, not from Google"],"f":["The caption of the header photo no longer spills out of its frame","On narrow screens the home header text no longer runs off the edge"]},"2026-10-12-v431":{"t":"Site audit: speed, search and translations","s":"I checked all 36 pages in four languages: links, translations, accessibility, speed on a slow phone and what ends up in search. Everything found is fixed.","n":[],"i":["Pages come alive sooner on phones: headings are fitted without extra layout passes, the reveal animation no longer slows loading, and the header clock no longer keeps the processor busy","Every page has its own description for search engines and social media again, and the home page has a clear title","Weather chart labels and source names in the October chronicle are translated into every language","Site search closes on the first press of Esc, and the e-mail address no longer ends up in the search index","The caption over the 3D model and the step labels are readable in either theme; the “Guests” block names the services that count visits"]},"2026-10-13-v45":{"t":"Fences, gates and a gas pipe in 3D","s":"The walk through the quarter is closer to the real street now: fences, gates with wickets, kerbs and a yellow gas pipe on posts line the houses.","n":["At houses 25–38 on Zarichna the fence type comes from the notes on the October 2011 panoramas: corrugated sheet, picket, concrete panels, hedges","On the other streets fences are picked by house type and marked as illustrative","You can no longer walk through fences: you stay on the street, as in real life"],"i":["The city, reconstruction and development pages are more compact: neighbouring blocks are grouped into tabs"]},"2026-10-14-v46":{"t":"Houses in 3D are now detailed","s":"Every house in the quarter got details: roof eaves, gable and hipped roofs, plinths, window sills, drainpipes, chimneys and doors with canopies. Apartment blocks now have balconies, entrance canopies and lift rooms on the roof.","n":["On Zarichna at houses 25–38 wall and roof colours and roof shapes come from the research table built on the 2011 panoramas","Some private houses have TV aerials and satellite dishes, as in 2011","The other details are illustrative and picked by building type"],"i":[]},"2026-10-14-v47":{"t":"Wires and benches on the streets of the 3D quarter","s":"Concrete poles with sagging wires now line the streets, with a wire running from them to every private house. Apartment entrances got benches, bushes grow in the yards and along the houses, gates have mailboxes, and the bigger roads have a centre line.","n":["Poles, wires, benches, bushes and mailboxes are illustrative: placed by street type, not from photos","On the walk you can't pass through poles and benches"],"i":[]},"2026-10-14-v48":{"t":"Cars, garages and a bus stop in the 3D quarter","s":"Cars in the colours of the time stand along the yard driveways and now and then by the houses. Rows of metal garages with doors in different colours appeared next to the apartment blocks. The avenue has a bus shelter and a kiosk, and washing dries in the yards of private houses.","n":["Cars, garages, the stop, the kiosk and the washing are illustrative: placed by the kind of place, not from photos","On the walk you can't pass through them"],"i":[]},"2026-10-14-v49":{"t":"Playgrounds in the yards of the apartment blocks","s":"The apartment blocks now have playgrounds with a sandpit, swings, a slide, a pull-up bar and a bench. Rubbish containers stand on a concrete pad by the end walls, and some balconies have satellite dishes. Cars look neater, with an underbody and wheels under the body.","n":["Playgrounds, containers and dishes are illustrative: placed by the kind of place, not from photos"],"i":[]},"2026-10-14-v50":{"t":"Fences by plot and traffic on the streets","s":"The fences of the 3D quarter were rebuilt from scratch. Every private house now has its own plot: a street fence with a gate and wicket, fences between neighbours and at the back. Corrugated sheet, picket fences, concrete sections with arches and lattice, brick gate pillars, a soil or gravel verge with a ragged asphalt edge and driveways to the gates. On Zarichna the gas pipe rises over every gate. Cars and a bus drive the streets: they keep their distance, give way at junctions and stop for the walker. Kerbs and pavements remain only on the avenues.","n":["On Zarichna at houses 25–38 the fence type, gate colour, the gravel verge on the west side and the driveway surface come from the notes on the October 2011 panoramas","The other fences, the cars and their movement are illustrative","The cars carry no number plates"],"i":[]},"2026-10-15-v51":{"t":"A cleaner 3D quarter: no walk mode, no stray models","s":"The walk mode is gone completely. Models with no source behind them left the scene: playgrounds, garages, the bus stop and kiosk, washing, bushes, benches, mailboxes, dishes and cars in the yards. What stays is what the 2011 panoramas show and what is typical of these streets: plot fences, gates, the gas pipe, concrete poles with wires and street lamps. Trees were redrawn with round crowns, poplars along the avenues and a fruit tree in the yard of each private house.","n":["The cars on the streets stay and are still illustrative","The model note was rewritten: what comes from sources and what is typical"],"i":[]},"2026-10-15-v52":{"t":"Trams on Dzerzhinsky Avenue","s":"The 3D quarter now has the tram line that really runs here: two tracks on their own bed in the middle of Dzerzhinsky Avenue, sleepers and rails, low kerbs, centre poles with arms to both tracks and street lamps, and an overhead wire above each track. Tatra T3SU cars run on it: one cab, three doors on the right, a pantograph. In 2011 routes 9 and 10 of depot No. 3 ran here.","n":["The line comes from OpenStreetMap and is aligned to the avenue's axis: in the OSM data it sits up to 3 m off the model's carriageways","The sources used show no stop inside the quarter, so the trams pass through without stopping","The cars wear the factory red-and-cream livery; the headway is shortened so a tram is more often in view","Cars on the avenue now keep to their side: the southern carriageway runs east, the northern one west"],"i":[]},"2026-10-16-v53":{"t":"Site audit: everything found is fixed","s":"The site went through a full check: 126 pages in four languages, on desktop and phone, in the light and dark themes. Everything it found is fixed.","n":["The radio on the Sounds page now plays real field recordings: rain, a Prague tram, a stadium in Vienna, the RWM time station, night wind and trains. Each station credits its author and licence","The updates feed no longer floods the counter with requests when it is down or blocked","A link to /en/, /uk/ or /fi/ always opens in the language it was sent in","The language switch is made of real links, so it also works without JavaScript","Search: when nothing turns up in this language, it shows matches in the other three","Game screenshots load at screen size: on a phone the Press page is about 1.5 MB lighter","The radio dial stations and atlas pins are easier to tap, and the atlas card links are readable in the dark theme","In the Guests block you can turn off counting your visits; the site then sends nothing to country.is or Abacus","The postcard slides out of its envelope again when reduced motion is on"],"i":[]},"2026-10-17-v531":{"t":"Time pips, to the standard","s":"The radio’s time-signal station now plays the six pips before the news as they were: 1000 Hz, 0.1 s each, one a second, the start of the sixth being the exact time. They follow your clock, the sixth falling on :00 and :30, and sound the way they did from the kitchen speaker of the wired radio.","n":[],"i":[]}};
